00:22:15.544 --> 00:22:16.924
DM: Well, whatever. It doesn't matter.

00:22:18.244 --> 00:22:18.324
Unknown: I don't know.

00:22:18.324 --> 00:22:20.444
DM: You could have, you can have told them where you are.

00:22:21.024 --> 00:22:21.024
Unknown: Fine.

00:22:21.044 --> 00:22:21.524
Unknown: It's fine.

00:22:24.164 --> 00:22:26.484
Kenzo: So, Dimitar, where do we want to fight these guys, fight the dragon?

00:22:27.724 --> 00:22:29.504
Kenzo: Is there any way to get, get it closer to ground?

00:22:31.104 --> 00:22:34.444
Delwath: So I think the simulacrum is potentially worth the risk.

00:22:34.444 --> 00:22:35.584
Seeker: What time of day is it right now?

00:22:36.124 --> 00:22:37.704
Delwath: It's like, what, 4:00 in the afternoon?

00:22:38.024 --> 00:22:40.604
DM: Like 5:00. It's like the hour before sunset.

00:22:41.124 --> 00:22:43.444
Seeker: So I could have it ready by dawn.

00:22:43.784 --> 00:22:44.044
Unknown: Yeah.

00:22:45.864 --> 00:22:47.624
Seeker: Do black dragons like to attack in the middle of the night?

00:22:47.744 --> 00:22:48.064
Unknown: Probably.

00:22:48.064 --> 00:22:49.184
Wellby: Can we do it from inside a tomb?

00:22:50.144 --> 00:22:53.264
Seeker: So I need to be near Delwath all, the entire time.

00:22:54.584 --> 00:22:54.704
Unknown: Yeah.

00:22:54.764 --> 00:22:56.604
Seeker: I need a pile of snow.

00:22:56.604 --> 00:22:57.764
Unknown: [laughs]

00:22:57.764 --> 00:22:57.864
Unknown: Snow?

00:22:57.864 --> 00:22:58.784
Seeker: And a lot of rubies.

00:22:59.344 --> 00:23:01.444
DM: You need a lot of rubies. Do you have any rubies?

00:23:02.284 --> 00:23:03.224
Seeker: Oh, I thought we still had a bunch

00:23:04.444 --> 00:23:05.224
Seeker: in the hole, don't we?

00:23:06.164 --> 00:23:07.124
Unknown: Uh, we can go check.

00:23:08.324 --> 00:23:12.404
Seeker: I believe that we determined that we're gonna be able to do simulacrum at least one more time.

00:23:12.404 --> 00:23:13.264
Unknown: I think you're right.

00:23:15.924 --> 00:23:16.484
Unknown: And I do have the-

00:23:16.524 --> 00:23:21.204
DM: But, but you also tried to restock on rubies and couldn't because the, uh-

00:23:21.704 --> 00:23:23.364
Seeker: We had consumed all available rubies.

00:23:23.364 --> 00:23:24.064
Unknown: [laughs]

00:23:24.104 --> 00:23:26.324
DM: Because Rizvan had consumed all available rubies.

00:23:27.784 --> 00:23:29.024
Unknown: Oh, Rizvan had.

00:23:29.024 --> 00:23:31.504
Delwath: Remember to make, to make Uz-Kakar

00:23:32.604 --> 00:23:34.564
Unknown: forever safe from undead.

00:23:34.564 --> 00:23:35.004
Seeker: Right.

00:23:37.204 --> 00:23:39.764
Seeker: There should be giant statues of us in that city, or at least of Rizvan.

00:23:39.784 --> 00:23:41.544
DM: There's a giant... There is a giant statue of Rizvan.

00:23:41.584 --> 00:23:43.384
Unknown: Yeah, they built one. Oh, right.

00:23:44.264 --> 00:23:46.124
Seeker: That's good and appropriate.

00:23:47.184 --> 00:23:49.904
Delwath: But the dragon will probably have some rubies

00:23:50.924 --> 00:23:52.884
Delwath: once we kill it. We can restock here.

00:23:53.204 --> 00:23:54.364
DM: Oh, yeah. No, that's right. You have-

00:23:54.384 --> 00:23:58.504
Wellby: And then go back in time and create the simulacrum.

00:23:58.504 --> 00:23:58.804
Wellby: [laughs]

00:23:58.824 --> 00:24:01.044
DM: You have the rubies from the elemental forge.

00:24:02.064 --> 00:24:02.524
Seeker: Amazing.

00:24:06.004 --> 00:24:09.504
Delwath: None of the materials in the divine forge were useful for this kind of-

00:24:09.564 --> 00:24:10.704
DM: No, it was all metal.

00:24:11.544 --> 00:24:11.824
Unknown: Yeah.

00:24:16.344 --> 00:24:16.484
Unknown: S- So

00:24:17.920 --> 00:24:19.460
Unknown: And purely out of

00:24:20.680 --> 00:24:26.940
Seeker: strategic concern for our own future wellbeing and not out of vanity, Delwath, you think it is a good idea to make another Delwath?

00:24:28.100 --> 00:24:38.200
Delwath: Yeah. 'Cause Fly, I mean, honestly, just having a Delwath literally doing nothing except casting Fly and hiding is very

00:24:38.240 --> 00:24:39.980
Delwath: useful because the problem with...

00:24:39.980 --> 00:24:44.680
Delwath: When I cast Fly, that's fine, but if I fail a concentration check, we plummet to the ground.

00:24:44.680 --> 00:24:46.140
Seeker: Everybody. Wellby and you at least.

00:24:46.140 --> 00:24:47.420
Unknown: Yeah.

00:24:47.420 --> 00:24:48.180
Seeker: And these guys-

00:24:48.520 --> 00:24:49.580
Delwath: They can fly on their own

00:24:49.580 --> 00:24:50.700
Seeker: ... have endless flying.

00:24:50.700 --> 00:24:54.200
Delwath: Yeah. But also by not, if I'm not using

00:24:55.220 --> 00:25:00.060
Unknown: Fly to fl- if I'm not using my concentration to fly, I can use my concentration to do other stuff.

00:25:00.620 --> 00:25:01.720
Seeker: And Fly affects-

00:25:02.760 --> 00:25:04.660
Delwath: If I cast at 5th level, it's three people.

00:25:04.660 --> 00:25:10.200
Seeker: 'Cause then we could get the, um, construct flying too, which would be pretty cool.

00:25:10.200 --> 00:25:12.460
Delwath: Either the construct or the...

00:25:12.480 --> 00:25:17.880
Delwath: I mean, the other thing is the, the second Delwath could cast Fly on himself,

00:25:19.280 --> 00:25:20.480
Delwath: Delwath Prime and Seeker,

00:25:21.720 --> 00:25:22.580
Delwath: and then could-

00:25:22.600 --> 00:25:23.700
Seeker: It gives us some options, basically.

00:25:23.700 --> 00:25:26.880
Delwath: Right. But also could throw spells from long range.

00:25:27.940 --> 00:25:29.440
Seeker: Which might even be more important.

00:25:29.440 --> 00:25:33.520
Delwath: Right. But to, to stay away so that, like, the dragon doesn't...

00:25:34.800 --> 00:25:38.400
Seeker: There needs to be a way to position these, the character figurines.

00:25:38.440 --> 00:25:41.300
Delwath: Oh, man. A second Delwath could cast Scatter also.

00:25:41.300 --> 00:25:41.920
Seeker: Cast what?

00:25:41.940 --> 00:25:42.500
Unknown: Scatter.

00:25:42.540 --> 00:25:43.040
Unknown: Ooh, yeah.

00:25:43.040 --> 00:25:43.800
Unknown: Two Scatters.

00:25:45.120 --> 00:25:48.100
Seeker: Yeah. [clears throat] All right, we should get to work on that.

00:25:48.220 --> 00:25:50.260
Delwath: Let's do it. I mean, you can't make one of yourself, can you?

00:25:50.880 --> 00:25:54.840
Seeker: I could-- I can, it's just not obviously better than the Delwath version.

00:25:55.000 --> 00:25:58.100
Delwath: Yeah, I think Delwath, I think the Delwath version is good, is a good plan.

00:25:59.880 --> 00:26:01.200
Seeker: Just because of the Fly spell.

00:26:01.200 --> 00:26:01.460
Unknown: That's what-

00:26:01.500 --> 00:26:04.060
Delwath: Yeah, I think Fly plus Scatter is pretty useful.

00:26:07.460 --> 00:26:09.420
Seeker: So the one remaining question being

00:26:11.500 --> 00:26:13.360
Seeker: if Dimitar has an ice machine anywhere.

00:26:14.820 --> 00:26:16.700
DM: Uh, Shape Water can freeze water.

00:26:17.480 --> 00:26:18.760
Seeker: Oh. Oh, oh, I can... Yeah, yeah.

00:26:18.820 --> 00:26:20.000
DM: Yeah, you have an ice machine.

00:26:20.000 --> 00:26:22.020
Unknown: On top of the canter. I am an ice machine.

00:26:22.020 --> 00:26:24.640
Unknown: Ice water. [chuckles] Shape Water.

00:26:24.640 --> 00:26:25.200
Seeker: We only need to run it-

00:26:25.240 --> 00:26:26.719
DM: Eat a little bit on the side.

00:26:27.920 --> 00:26:28.379
Unknown: What's that?

00:26:28.379 --> 00:26:29.740
DM: Eat a little bit on the side.

00:26:29.740 --> 00:26:31.960
Seeker: [chuckles] Snow cone, yeah.

00:26:31.960 --> 00:26:32.380
Unknown: Delicious.

00:26:35.980 --> 00:26:36.880
Seeker: All right, so...

00:26:38.520 --> 00:26:40.100
Delwath: I, I think we hide in the tunnel.

00:26:40.100 --> 00:26:40.340
Unknown: Yeah.

00:26:40.800 --> 00:26:41.960
Delwath: Let's try it. I mean,

00:26:43.640 --> 00:26:48.000
Delwath: if we get attacked at 3:00 AM before the simulacrum is ready, then we do.

00:26:48.080 --> 00:26:49.540
Seeker: Yeah. It's worth a try.

00:26:50.360 --> 00:26:51.060
Delwath: But also, like,

00:26:53.280 --> 00:26:56.220
Unknown: it's unclear exactly what the mechanism of...

00:26:57.500 --> 00:27:00.060
Unknown: What's she gonna do? Can she even fit in the temple to sit?

00:27:02.620 --> 00:27:04.500
DM: She could probably crack the roof.

00:27:04.540 --> 00:27:07.200
Seeker: Right. Or flood the tunnel with acid or something.

00:27:07.200 --> 00:27:10.780
Unknown: Yeah.

00:27:10.880 --> 00:27:12.300
Unknown: But she won't be able to get by the ladder.

00:27:13.740 --> 00:27:15.560
DM: She's quite a bit bigger than the ladder.

00:27:15.840 --> 00:27:16.520
Unknown: That's true.

00:27:16.520 --> 00:27:17.620
DM: Be a little bit less of a-

00:27:18.420 --> 00:27:22.340
Seeker: Right. [chuckles] Um, all right.

00:27:22.340 --> 00:27:22.860
Unknown: So Seeker

00:27:23.940 --> 00:27:26.080
Seeker: begin-- drinks the potion of watchful rest.

00:27:27.320 --> 00:27:27.380
DM: Yep.

00:27:27.460 --> 00:27:28.500
Unknown: Begins the process of...

00:27:29.400 --> 00:27:31.220
Seeker: Oh, that's interesting.

00:27:32.360 --> 00:27:33.300
Seeker: There's this sort of like

00:27:34.740 --> 00:27:36.040
Seeker: rules situation here.

00:27:37.800 --> 00:27:41.180
Seeker: Do I have a spell slot that I can use to cast simula- simulacrum?

00:27:42.460 --> 00:27:42.800
DM: Oh-

00:27:42.900 --> 00:27:43.120
Unknown: Or the-

00:27:43.320 --> 00:27:45.300
DM: Oh no, you don't have any spell slots.

00:27:45.340 --> 00:27:45.360
Unknown: Oh.

00:27:45.880 --> 00:27:48.040
Delwath: You don't have a 7th or 8th level slot, do you?

00:27:49.480 --> 00:27:50.020
DM: No, you don't.

00:27:50.040 --> 00:27:51.540
Seeker: Circle of Power can't fix that, can it?

00:27:51.600 --> 00:27:52.420
DM: No, it can't.

00:27:52.420 --> 00:27:53.340
Unknown: No, we can't do this.

00:27:53.420 --> 00:27:53.820
Unknown: Fuck.

00:27:55.100 --> 00:27:56.200
Seeker: It was such a good idea.

00:27:58.520 --> 00:28:00.200
DM: You used it for Teleport, so y-

00:28:00.540 --> 00:28:02.100
Seeker: Oh, I was like, "I have a 7th level slot."

00:28:02.100 --> 00:28:02.540
Seeker: No, we just teleported.

00:28:02.540 --> 00:28:03.580
DM: You used it to teleport.

00:28:03.580 --> 00:28:03.680
Unknown: We just teleported.

00:28:03.780 --> 00:28:04.480
DM: Yeah.

00:28:04.540 --> 00:28:05.560
Unknown: Yeah.

00:28:05.560 --> 00:28:07.240
DM: So that doesn't work, unfortunately.

00:28:09.240 --> 00:28:09.580
Unknown: Ah.

00:28:13.700 --> 00:28:15.260
Seeker: No Delwath Prime. Sorry, buddy.

00:28:15.920 --> 00:28:16.580
Unknown: That's all right.

00:28:16.860 --> 00:28:19.220
Wellby: I think we should long rest, like, immediately.

00:28:19.480 --> 00:28:19.920
Unknown: Yeah, that's probably-

00:28:19.960 --> 00:28:21.540
Unknown: So we're ready to go at 3:00 AM.

00:28:21.780 --> 00:28:22.700
Unknown: Yeah, I think you're right.

00:28:24.380 --> 00:28:24.600
DM: Okay.

00:28:25.940 --> 00:28:26.740
DM: You all go to sleep.

00:28:27.620 --> 00:28:29.180
Wellby: Vision, Jay, Han.

00:28:29.380 --> 00:28:30.920
DM: Take... Yep. Take turns-

00:28:31.580 --> 00:28:31.620
Unknown: Yeah.

00:28:31.620 --> 00:28:32.800
DM: Take turns watching.

00:28:32.880 --> 00:28:33.140
Unknown: Yep.

00:28:33.920 --> 00:28:36.579
Delwath: I'm gonna set, um, my links out too.

00:28:36.720 --> 00:28:41.260
DM: Oh, yeah. Just set your links to guard instead of you actually watching so she doesn't see anything.

00:28:43.840 --> 00:28:44.120
DM: Okay.

00:28:44.180 --> 00:28:45.860
Unknown: Maybe.

00:28:45.900 --> 00:28:46.620
Wellby: It's awesome.

00:28:46.620 --> 00:28:47.220
DM: So close.

00:28:47.600 --> 00:28:48.180
Unknown: It does. It's so good.

00:28:48.180 --> 00:28:51.000
DM: Keep it in mind for another time, maybe for the Apollyon fight.

00:28:52.900 --> 00:28:53.100
Unknown: Right.

00:28:53.100 --> 00:28:53.240
DM: Or-

00:28:54.000 --> 00:28:54.660
Seeker: The thing is,

00:28:56.280 --> 00:28:57.600
Seeker: do one that wander around the ship.

00:28:57.600 --> 00:28:59.380
Seeker: The simulacrum can just hang out.

00:28:59.860 --> 00:29:00.340
Unknown: Yeah.

00:29:00.360 --> 00:29:00.700
Unknown: It doesn't like-

00:29:00.760 --> 00:29:02.420
DM: Right. But it doesn't heal, so it...

00:29:02.420 --> 00:29:07.680
DM: And it can't really gain spell slots, so you gotta, like, be judicious about when you actually use it.

00:29:07.960 --> 00:29:08.520
Unknown: Right.

00:29:08.540 --> 00:29:11.740
DM: Yeah, but you could prep- prepare one on the ship and...

00:29:11.740 --> 00:29:11.980
DM: Yeah.

00:29:14.100 --> 00:29:19.740
DM: Okay, so as you drift off to sleep, um, you all find yourself in a shared dream.

00:29:20.920 --> 00:29:21.920
DM: Um, you are,

00:29:23.460 --> 00:29:26.820
DM: uh... The first thing you see is something you've seen before.

00:29:26.820 --> 00:29:27.420
DM: It's the,

00:29:28.660 --> 00:29:28.960
DM: um,

00:29:30.700 --> 00:29:41.320
DM: standing on top of a high mountain pass, this massive shadow dragon above you, and then Rai, like, everybody fighting.

00:29:41.340 --> 00:29:43.140
DM: I don't remember what everybody was doing.

00:29:43.920 --> 00:29:45.560
DM: Bar- Beryl had a quarterstaff, right?

00:29:45.760 --> 00:29:46.080
Unknown: Yeah.

00:29:46.080 --> 00:29:46.360
DM: Okay.

00:29:47.680 --> 00:29:49.760
DM: You know, Beryl's fighting with a quarterstaff.

00:29:50.320 --> 00:29:53.320
DM: I, I think Aaron had, like, some weird shadow dagger.

00:29:53.660 --> 00:29:54.960
DM: Something like that.

00:29:54.960 --> 00:29:55.180
DM: Um,

00:29:57.400 --> 00:30:07.680
DM: and then the moment when Shamut dies and there's this, like, silent flash that goes across the world, and then suddenly you're yanked

00:30:07.680 --> 00:30:10.280
DM: as Rai teleports to Drankor.

00:30:12.020 --> 00:30:15.760
DM: And you see what you haven't seen before, which is that, um,

00:30:17.080 --> 00:30:22.296
DM: standing right outside this, there's this elaborate tomb,

00:30:23.476 --> 00:30:32.896
DM: a structure, um, in which you gather Apollyon is buried, and there's a dagger flying towards the door.

00:30:34.536 --> 00:30:35.736
DM: And Rai

00:30:36.876 --> 00:30:40.696
DM: grabs it in his hand moments before it strikes the door

00:30:42.776 --> 00:30:43.836
DM: and stands there.

00:30:44.776 --> 00:30:47.336
DM: And time flashes forward, and you are

00:30:48.796 --> 00:30:55.576
DM: in Rai's mind as he probes these bindings, trying to understand what he's grabbed onto.

00:30:56.456 --> 00:31:03.356
DM: And he reaches through the various tangles and twists and knots of Cha'mutte's magic,

00:31:04.476 --> 00:31:04.876
DM: of

00:31:06.516 --> 00:31:12.416
DM: the essence of the plane of Limbo, the plane of chaos that Cha'mutte was close to,

00:31:13.356 --> 00:31:16.496
DM: woven in knots into a net

00:31:17.796 --> 00:31:19.316
DM: that hel- that holds

00:31:20.656 --> 00:31:21.896
DM: Apollyon in place.

00:31:22.356 --> 00:31:25.275
Seeker: This is like one moment that Kong should not be asleep.

00:31:26.496 --> 00:31:26.956
DM: Are you good?

00:31:26.956 --> 00:31:27.716
Unknown: I'm still awake.

00:31:27.716 --> 00:31:27.936
DM: Okay.

00:31:27.976 --> 00:31:28.336
Unknown: All right.

00:31:29.896 --> 00:31:30.096
DM: Um,

00:31:32.836 --> 00:31:39.736
DM: and this net wraps all the way around the tomb, and it's woven tightly, but there are,

00:31:40.756 --> 00:31:43.936
DM: uh, still small holes where

00:31:45.476 --> 00:31:48.576
DM: something could, could pierce through and could penetrate.

00:31:50.156 --> 00:31:52.816
DM: But Rai realizes as long as the dagger is held,

00:31:55.296 --> 00:31:58.416
DM: Apollyon has no power to do anything.

00:32:00.436 --> 00:32:05.156
DM: And time passes, and Apollyon seems to grow weaker every year in which he cannot

00:32:08.256 --> 00:32:12.256
DM: feed on souls, cannot strengthen himself with his dagger.

00:32:13.936 --> 00:32:14.416
DM: He must have been-

00:32:14.436 --> 00:32:16.276
Kenzo: And Rai's just standing there outside of Holian?

00:32:16.576 --> 00:32:24.016
DM: Yeah, so far. He must have been weak to begin with and grows weaker and weaker.

00:32:24.016 --> 00:32:30.896
DM: [laughs] I have to look at that later.

00:32:30.896 --> 00:32:34.016
DM: Isaac just texted me, "Our session notes are better than yours."

00:32:34.176 --> 00:32:34.716
Seeker: Oh, geez.

00:32:35.896 --> 00:32:36.116
DM: Um,

00:32:38.576 --> 00:32:38.916
DM: grows--

00:32:40.036 --> 00:32:42.896
DM: feels him grow weaker and weaker as the,

00:32:44.196 --> 00:32:49.016
DM: um, as he grows, the years pass and the connection to

00:32:50.936 --> 00:32:59.196
DM: the souls trapped in this dagger grows dimmer and dimmer over decades, until Rai eventually decides

00:33:01.196 --> 00:33:02.556
DM: standing here

00:33:04.696 --> 00:33:11.276
DM: is maybe not the best place to be, the dagger so close, and of course, he can't move except by teleporting because he's all jade.

00:33:12.056 --> 00:33:12.916
DM: He teleports

00:33:15.556 --> 00:33:15.876
DM: to

00:33:17.396 --> 00:33:22.996
DM: a-- an-- the one area in Dranikor that seems not cursed by

00:33:25.596 --> 00:33:29.616
DM: sh- by the pla- by the echoes of the plague and the,

00:33:30.516 --> 00:33:30.716
DM: uh,

00:33:31.896 --> 00:33:37.336
DM: dark energy of Apollyon and all of the many, many, many people who died here.

00:33:37.336 --> 00:33:45.176
DM: It's the grand-- it's a grand, huge domed building, a temple to the eight divines.

00:33:46.996 --> 00:33:57.216
DM: Eight sort of alcoves stretching out, um, to create these separate spaces for eight, uh, eight gods to be worshiped around this giant

00:33:57.216 --> 00:33:58.096
DM: central dome.

00:33:59.916 --> 00:34:01.516
Seeker: It's the same as the pantheon on this side.

00:34:02.316 --> 00:34:03.136
Unknown: It's the same as the eight gods.

00:34:03.236 --> 00:34:04.656
DM: Uh, it's the same eight gods.

00:34:04.656 --> 00:34:10.456
DM: Yeah, yeah, yeah. The, the architecture is a little different, and you actually recognize this as where you saw

00:34:11.856 --> 00:34:19.836
DM: Kenzo had a dream where the, um, the awakened soul monks found Rai, and this is the building.

00:34:19.836 --> 00:34:21.076
DM: And Dimitar is there as well.

00:34:22.336 --> 00:34:22.536
DM: Um,

00:34:25.536 --> 00:34:26.656
DM: and over the years,

00:34:27.576 --> 00:34:33.076
DM: a hundred years pass, and Apollyon seems to grow weaker and weaker, but this

00:34:35.076 --> 00:34:36.356
DM: net of chaos,

00:34:37.496 --> 00:34:37.896
DM: this

00:34:39.196 --> 00:34:43.916
DM: fragment of Limbo that's wrapped around the temple seems to grow stronger and stronger.

00:34:45.696 --> 00:34:50.536
DM: And it seems like there's tendrils from it reaching out across the world.

00:34:52.416 --> 00:34:59.756
DM: And as Apollyon grows weaker and the chaos of Limbo grows stronger, Rai makes a decision

00:35:01.636 --> 00:35:06.596
DM: that perhaps the only way forward-- that if he does nothing,

00:35:08.056 --> 00:35:11.736
DM: then this curse that Cha'mutte left behind may grow too strong.

00:35:14.716 --> 00:35:15.916
DM: And so he leaves the dagger

00:35:19.456 --> 00:35:25.656
